# Changes

Revision history for Perl module Paubox_Email_SDK / Paubox_Forms_SDK.

This file is Markdown so that release-please can maintain it. The filename is
kept for CPAN convention; release-please is configured with
`changelog-path: CHANGES`.

## [2.0.0](https://github.com/Paubox/paubox-perl/compare/v1.2.0...v2.0.0) (2026-08-21)


### ⚠ BREAKING CHANGES

* the version scheme moves from Perl decimal versions to three-part semver, and the next version has to be 2.0.0. Perl compares the repo's previous 1.5 as v1.500.0, so no 1.x.y semver is greater than it and PAUSE would reject anything smaller as a downgrade. release-please only emits three-part semver, so 2.0.0 is the smallest number that satisfies both. The major bump reflects that constraint, not a break in the API surface.

### Changes

First release since 1.2 in July 2019. It carries everything previously listed
under `1.3`, `1.4` and `1.5` — none of those versions was ever uploaded to
CPAN, so they ship together here.

- Removed the username / endpoint name from API authentication. Authentication
  is now by API key alone; `API_USERNAME` is no longer read from `config.cfg`
- Changed the API base URL host to `api.paubox.com` for both APIs. The Email
  API is now `https://api.paubox.com/v1` (was
  `https://api.paubox.net/v1/{apiUsername}`) and the Forms API is now
  `https://api.paubox.com/forms` (was `https://apx.paubox.com/forms`)
- Added `Paubox_Forms_SDK` with `getForm` and `submitForm`
- Added authenticated form-management methods to `Paubox_Forms_SDK`:
  `listForms`, `getFormById`, `createForm`, `updateForm`, `archiveForm`,
  `unarchiveForm`, `copyForm`, `getFormStats`, `listFormSubmissions`,
  `getSubmissionsCsv`, `getSubmissionPdf`
- Added scoped API key authentication for the Forms API (`Authorization:
  Bearer`). Pass `apiKey` to `Paubox_Forms_SDK->new()` or set `FORMS_API_KEY`
  in `config.cfg`. Keys must include the `forms` scope. Public `getForm` and
  `submitForm` are unchanged and still require no credentials
- Extended `Paubox_Email_SDK::ApiHelper` with `callToAPIByPut` and a
  `responseCode` accessor storing the HTTP status of the instance's last
  request, used by the CSV and PDF export methods
- Updated `ApiHelper` to set the `Authorization` header conditionally, enabling
  use with the public no-auth Forms endpoints
- Added a URL path-segment sanitizer to `Paubox_Forms_SDK`. Caller-supplied
  `form_id` and `submission_id` values are rejected when they contain `/`, `?`,
  `#`, newlines, or the dot-segments `.` and `..`; authenticated methods
  additionally require UUID shape. Prevents a hostile identifier from
  retargeting the request on the same host with the caller's bearer token
  attached
- Set an explicit 30-second `REST::Client` timeout in `ApiHelper`, previously
  inheriting `LWP::UserAgent`'s 180-second default; hung connections now abort
  promptly

